	(footprint "aiee:CAP-ADJ-TH_2P-BD7.5_5602"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "a6a84148-0823-4e8d-9b63-bd11bf0771cd")
		(at 46.135 24.8125 180)
		(descr "Johanson Manufacturing (Knowles) 5602 air-dielectric trimmer capacitor, DigiKey 1956-1000-ND (5602 IS the complete orderable MPN, not a series prefix - confirmed on the DigiKey product page, no suffix scheme). 1-30 pF, 250 VDC (500 VDC test), -65 to +125 C, top screwdriver-slot adjust, panel/PCB-mount threaded case, Q>800 @ 100 MHz. Source: Knowles combined trimmer catalog (mm.digikey.com/.../KnowlesTrimmersCatalogueweb177409287.pdf), 'Air Trimmers' dimension page, part-pair row '5600/5602', Figure 4 (5602's own drawing) cross-checked against Figure 3 (5600, near-identical body, clearer lead dimensioning) and the DigiKey parametric page. TWO PHYSICAL TERMINALS: (1) the threaded case/bushing (.234-64 UNS-2A thread, nominal major dia 5.94mm, catalog dim table col (UNS-2A); overall body/hex-collar envelope dia 6.99-7.49mm, catalog col C) - the FIXED, non-rotating structure that mounts through the board and carries the top screwdriver-slot tuning access; (2) a separate insulated .015in (0.38mm) lead wire, catalog-dimensioned as exiting near the case base offset ~0.09in (2.29mm) from the body axis (Fig 3, the clearer of the two drawings for this dimension - Fig 4's own equivalent offset is drawn but its H/J/F/K sub-dimensions could not be resolved to certainty from the scanned catalog, so this footprint's PAD-2 position (see below) is this librarian's OWN clearance-driven placement, not a transcribed factory offset - the 0.38mm lead is flexible and hand-formable at this build's qty-5 scale, matching this project's existing precedent for R1's tab-lap 'measure and confirm' step, see parts/T50R0-250-12X.json). NET ASSIGNMENT IS PHYSICAL, NOT INFERRED (state.json P3 decision, 2026-08-09): PAD 1 = the threaded case/hex-collar assembly -> GND. PAD 2 = the insulated lead wire -> RF. A panel-mount trimmer's case is engineered to pass through a grounded metal panel, so the case is the ground-compatible terminal by construction; the case is also the only terminal a hand or tool actually brushes during tuning, so it is the terminal that must be grounded whatever its internal (rotor/stator) role is - this makes 'exposed metal is at ground' true regardless of which plate physically moves. PAD 1 sized as a solder-in plated hole (drill 6.30mm clears the 5.94mm nominal thread major dia with ~0.18mm radial clearance for hand assembly; pad copper 7.60mm dia lands the full hex-collar shoulder, no panel nut required for this qty-5 board - the nut is optional hardware, not modelled). PAD 2 sized generously for the 0.38mm lead (drill 0.80mm, pad 1.60mm dia). Pad centres 6.00mm apart (this librarian's own layout choice, not a catalog dimension) giving 1.40mm edge-to-edge copper clearance between the two different-net pads, comfortably inside the board's 0.80mm HV floor (constraints.json, IPC-2221 A6, 101-150V band at 122.5 Vpeak). Silk kept >=0.25mm clear of all copper. F.Fab circle at 7.49mm dia is the catalog's max body/hex-collar envelope (col C); the small F.Fab cross at pad 1 centre marks the tuning-slot recess. TOOL: Johanson 8764, .130in (3.30mm) shank, non-metallic tip preferred (confirmed tool P/N for the 56xx family, Knowles catalog p.2 tool cross-reference table, cited in research/components.md). TOP-SIDE PLACEMENT ONLY: the tuning slot faces away from the board on the F.Cu side; do not mirror this footprint to the back copper layer.")
		(tags "trimmer variable capacitor RF top-adjust Johanson air-dielectric panel-mount")
		(property "Reference" "C1"
