	(footprint "aiee:MountingHole_3.2mm_M3_Pad_5.0mm"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "f07cb617-2aef-4a76-a4fd-aed2d6e859de")
		(at 27.235 34.3125)
		(descr "aiee local clone of stock MountingHole:MountingHole_3.2mm_M3_Pad with the copper PAD shrunk from 6.4mm to 5.0mm diameter (drill unchanged at 3.2mm, annular ring 0.9mm - comfortably above the JLC/fab floors min_annular_width 0.15mm and min_through_hole_diameter 0.3mm). Reason: placelib's placement-legality extent is `declared courtyard UNION pad-field bbox+0.25mm`, and for a circular THT pad that union is ALWAYS a square of side pad_diameter+0.5mm regardless of the courtyard's own size (a circle can never contain the padded bbox square) - LEARNINGS 2026-08-09 [placement][geometry][python]. The stock 6.4mm pad therefore claims a 6.9mm square footprint per mounting hole; on this board's 26x20mm outline that makes H1-H3 unplaceable flanking R1 (R1's own pad-field extent is a 14.2x7.5mm rectangle, and two 6.9mm-square holes cannot fit beside it on a 26mm edge). Dropping the pad to 5.0mm (<=5.35mm, where the placement inequality closes) restores feasibility with no outline change and no loss of M3 clearance-hole function (5.0mm pad on a 3.2mm drill is still a generous clearance annulus for an M3 screw head/washer bearing surface). Courtyard scaled proportionally to the same margin convention as the stock part (pad radius + 0.25mm: stock 3.2+0.25=3.45mm radius, here 2.5+0.25=2.75mm radius).")
		(tags "mountinghole M3 aiee pad-reduced")
		(property "Reference" "H1"
			(at 0 -3.425 0)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
			(uuid "221e8d1a-4cfd-4b4c-b39d-b29cda184c91")
